<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35724" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνίπτω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνίψω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					7.447
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠνίπᾰπε [ῑ</span>] <i><span class="en">
				2.245
			</span></i>, al., also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνένιπε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					15.546
				</span></i>
			, al. (with vv. ll. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνένισπεν,
				ἐνένιπτεν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.321
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.473
			</span></i>):— 
				Ep.
			 Verb (once in <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i> (v. infr.)), <i>reprove, upbraid,</i> freq. with words
			added to strengthen the sense, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλεπῷ ἠνίπαπε μύθῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.245
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλεποῖσιν ὀνείδεσι θυμὸν ἔνιπτε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					3.438
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνένιπεν ὀνειδείοις ἐπέεσσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					18.326
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν δ᾽ αἰσχρῶς ἐνένιπε</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				321
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.473
			</span></i>; or simply 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόσιν δ᾽ ἠνίπαπε μύθῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					3.427
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κραδίην ἠνίπαπε μύθῳ</span>
			<i>reproved</i> his soul with words, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				20.17
			</span></i>: without a modal word, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ τίς με
				καὶ ἄλλος ἐνίπτοι</span> were another <i>to attack</i>
			me, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.768
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόν ῥ᾽ Ἕκτωρ ἐνένιπεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					15.552
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				546
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καί τίς μ᾽ ἐνίπτων εἶπε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					590
				</span></i>
			: without acc., <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.78
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				24.161
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> after <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνέπω</span>
			, <i>tell, announce,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁδείας ἐνίπτων ἐλπίδας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					4.201
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				27.59
			</span></i>. Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνίσσω.</span></div>
